silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_concrete_anchor_4#nonequalitywitnesscell silm:hasLongDescription "The NonEqualityWitnessCell is The blank cell in the upper-right of the R3 tikzcd grid is not decorative: it is the diagrammatic carrier of the non-equality DomesticCat != TaxRow_TSN183798. Were the cell filled with an identification arrow, the probe would FAIL. The intentional emptiness records that the classification node (DomesticCat) and the taxonomy-source node (TaxRow_TSN183798 for Mittens, the Silver Spring resident cat owned by Mrs. Henderson) sit on opposite sides of the colimit apex Mittens and are connected only through Mittens, never directly. This is the geometric statement of probe R3." .
